\pard\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 1. Executive summary\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 From at least 4 September 2026 until the afternoon of 11 November 2026 (Asia/Manila), unauthenticated visitors could download application log files from the production web root. The largest file, /logs/cron.log, was about 22 MB. The same scan found other logs, the setup script, README, and Composer inventory also returning HTTP 200.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 The production .env file itself was not downloadable (HTTP 302 to login). .git was blocked (HTTP 403). No evidence in this scan showed mailbox passwords or APP_KEY in the public logs; the logs did expose operational detail (absolute paths, mail host, whether mail is enabled, queue depths, process names and timestamps).\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Containment is in place as of 14:10 Asia/Manila on 11 November 2026. Visiting https://lokafleet.dictr2.cloud/logs/cron.log now returns HTTP 302 to the login page. Cron jobs still run; their output is written beside the site root (app_logs), not under public_html.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs28 \cf2 1.1 Outcome at a glance\b0\par\pard\par\trowd\trgaph70\trpaddl70\trpaddr70 \cellx4500 \cellx9000
