\pard\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 2. Scope and method of the damage scan\b0\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs28 \cf2 2.1 In scope\b0\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Production site https://lokafleet.dictr2.cloud (A record 187.77.150.203).\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Unauthenticated HTTP GET of likely-sensitive paths (logs, env, git, setup, README, vendor metadata, health, PHP under config/).\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? On-server inspection: file modes, ownership, nginx/php-fpm/varnish process users, crontab, log locations.\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Application-code review of routing, file-view, cron HTTP endpoint, migrate.php, session path, and .htaccess.\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Cache behaviour (CloudPanel Varnish 512 MB).\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs28 \cf2 2.2 Out of scope\b0\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Full penetration test and authenticated abuse of every role.\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Copying or publishing log bodies, environment values, or credentials in this document.\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Forensic recovery of every IP that downloaded cron.log (access.log exists; not mined in this pass).\par\pard\sa60\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 \u8226? Staging (lokastage) except as a comparison of env file location.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs28 \cf2 2.3 How the scan was run\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Each URL was requested with curl without following redirects first, recording HTTP status, byte size, content-type, and the first bytes of the body. A second pass used cache-busting query strings and a Varnish purge. After mitigation, the same URLs were re-probed, including after the next 2-minute cron cycle.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 On the server, namei, process lists, php-fpm pool user (lokafleet_main), nginx workers, and varnishd were inspected. A chmod-000 experiment on setup.sh still returned HTTP 200 until the file bytes themselves changed, proving cache then proving live nginx can read the document root as root.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 3. Damage scan results (before mitigation)\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 First live probe on 11 November 2026, about 13:50\u8211?13:58 Asia/Manila. Sizes are download bytes.\par\pard\par\trowd\trgaph70\trpaddl70\trpaddr70 \cellx2250 \cellx4500 \cellx6750 \cellx9000
