\pard\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 4. Root cause\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 1. Cron jobs redirect stdout into public_html/logs (document root). The shell creates those files as ordinary static files.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 2. CloudPanel nginx treats existing files as static downloads. There is no location /logs/ \{ deny all; \} in the vhost.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 3. public_html/.htaccess denies .log and /logs/, but the site is nginx, not Apache.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 4. nginx workers for the public listener run as root. File mode 600 or directory mode 770 cannot hide a file still under the document root.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 5. Varnish (malloc, 512 MB) caches large static responses. Tightening permissions without a purge left the old 22 MB body in cache.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 6. PHP-FPM runs as lokafleet_main and can still write logs. Moving files out of public_html (or deleting them from the docroot) is the control that actually works.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Net: the application believed Apache .htaccess would protect logs. Production is nginx as root plus Varnish. Protection has to be \u8220?file is not in the web tree\u8221? (and ideally an nginx deny), not chmod.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 5. Mitigation steps (as performed)\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Failed attempts (do not rely on these alone): clpctl permissions reset 770/660 still HTTP 200 due to Varnish and root nginx; chmod 000 on setup.sh still served from cache; chmod 600 on a new cron.log still 200; uploading git index.php wholesale caused HTTP 500 because prod is missing channels/SSO files \u8212? reverted.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs28 \cf2 5.2 Controls that worked\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 A. Scan and keep evidence. Purge Varnish after every change: clpctl varnish-cache:purge --purge=all.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 B. Create app_logs beside public_html (not inside it). Move public_html/logs/*.log there. Leave the logs directory so a crontab redirect does not fail the PHP command, but do not keep .log files there.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 C. Deploy public_html/includes/harden_logs.php: umask 027; LOKA_LOG_DIR = sibling app_logs; CLI output buffering writes to app_logs; unlink leftover public_html/logs/*.log on every PHP request.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 D. migrate.php CLI-only 403. Overwrite setup.sh, README.md, .env.example in the docroot (unlink was not possible from a 755 directory). Blank vendor/composer/installed.json to []. Add Apache deny rules for local/XAMPP.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 E. file-view.php extra requireAuth(); session path prefers LOKA_LOG_DIR/sessions; production error_log under LOKA_LOG_DIR.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 F. Purge Varnish. curl without -L: 302 and 0 bytes for /logs/cron.log. Wait for next cron; confirm public logs has no *.log while app_logs/cron.log gains a new stanza. Confirm login HTTP 200.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs28 \cf2 5.3 Code files changed\b0\par\pard\par\trowd\trgaph70\trpaddl70\trpaddr70 \cellx4500 \cellx9000
