\pard\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 On disk after 14:10 cron: public_html/logs contained .htaccess, index.html, rates/, sessions/ \u8212? no *.log files. app_logs/cron.log received the queue processor finished stanza. A browser request to /logs/cron.log renders the LOKA login screen.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 7. Impact assessment\b0\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Confidentiality: High for operations metadata, low-to-medium for secrets. An unauthenticated party could learn internal paths, that Gmail SMTP is used, that mail is enabled, and historic queue health. Mailbox passwords and APP_KEY were not shown in the sampled public log lines.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Integrity: No evidence an outsider wrote files or changed data. World-writable PHP remains a local-user risk on a multi-site VPS.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Availability: Login returned HTTP 500 for a few minutes when git index.php was uploaded; rolled back. After rollback, login 200 and cron 14:10 completed.\par\pard\sa120\sl360\slmult1 \fs22 Accountability: nginx access logs can be searched for GET /logs/cron.log between 4 September 2026 and 11 November 2026 14:04 Asia/Manila.\par\pard\sa160\sl360\slmult1 \b \fs36 \cf2 8. Residual risk and recommended follow-up\b0\par\pard\par\trowd\trgaph70\trpaddl70\trpaddr70 \cellx3000 \cellx6000 \cellx9000
